{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_49f9fbd62a87eb4fc6debc663d14c1ad79df1f18480a892b9731ed7f5c1fdd05","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"linghungegeg/linghun@05d8457bd04a snapshot 64bad13006da78ed","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_dd3553a0f74aa2fa55ebd062c06c5af89a71d4b07be780783a4e9bf7785c78d7"],"source_ids":["src_90afde0e64ba5311b83808a4a90ed8ad"],"text":"API keys are stored by default in a user-level private provider.env outside the project; configuration precedence is shell environment variables, then provider.env, then project/default settings.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_576e25eef5c87199f9db080e6fe52691f59352e8af40aff6c45650f530af0c0b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"linghungegeg/linghun@05d8457bd04a snapshot 64bad13006da78ed","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36fe71d1db959bc49d75b6099f4ed6cd496f4dde853cb5caa84f6dd3b573cd26","slc_9e2491806fdebfda6d47ee4fdc9ba284bdd2a532a7c2b22b9c010052f1d1d98f"],"source_ids":["src_90afde0e64ba5311b83808a4a90ed8ad"],"text":"The design philosophy places key constraints at the system layer rather than in prompts: tool execution, permissions, evidence, verification, Git, indexing, caching, and failure learning form one main chain.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_59057bff1521de1b2fa4b2c439ab621a87f3d975d8a8ac95d7d7221731a0e985","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"linghungegeg/linghun@05d8457bd04a snapshot 64bad13006da78ed","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_60979791c02aad68d2e5a6b0ef2db09dde374dac8e491db8576671a6bdc355f8","slc_b670b555fe0395d769889269ae8a2206aa4eb1a93977f08a6ea7696e40f8ba28"],"source_ids":["src_90afde0e64ba5311b83808a4a90ed8ad"],"text":"The App Bridge currently supports only a Local HTTP Connector: transport must be http and baseUrl must be loopback (localhost, 127.0.0.1, or [::1]); external apps implement GET /linghun/capabilities and POST /linghun/execute, validated via /apps validate and connected via /apps connect.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7b25ad77dd48817528f587ebd28b2b03b3fe1b3f85706b3e765502bb6b5880e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"linghungegeg/linghun@05d8457bd04a snapshot 64bad13006da78ed","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_acabccb760432e113577cc4050569a00040563d2ab7b8bdc4b247600867af92d"],"source_ids":["src_90afde0e64ba5311b83808a4a90ed8ad"],"text":"Workflow Matrix decomposes complex goals into phase, slice, role, risk hint, runtime proposal, and evidence requirement, reusing /job, /fork, /agents, verification, and Git stable-point suggestions at the execution layer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9499e3bc21ee02dc53feffca3a2aec0cde6969986b826abe5e9e558ad16c45e4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"linghungegeg/linghun@05d8457bd04a snapshot 64bad13006da78ed","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2067a049d324d6163c708e5bfc6c04665f414bd16845f0197efdd2c8bede860b","slc_77713ae5e2fe976794163174d1488a81d28be8a842d1f03392397b2de8cf6e0e","slc_e92485adc0b82012a933ccc5f243e07cae1fe1eaf3abb7843268616b3476bca5"],"source_ids":["src_07b78b81c1b45a21bfd7ff09f120b1a6"],"text":"Repository development practice: an internal execution-plan document mandates strict phase ordering (phases 0-7), per-phase minimal verification, independent re-checks, recorded completed/blocked items, and forbids skipping phases or substituting hidden text fixes for underlying event fixes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e30c2089428e46049722c3145813b3c3"}
